          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Chinese court rules AI cost-cutting is not legal grounds to fire workers, setting landmark precedent",
            "articleSection": "Job Evolution",
            "abstract": "A court in Hangzhou, China has ruled that a fintech company acted illegally when it dismissed a 35-year-old employee on the grounds that an AI replacement would be cheaper, rejecting the argument that cost savings from automation justify termination. The worker, surnamed Zhou, had overseen AI-generated responses and was offered a demotion and pay cut before being fired for refusing. The ruling is being watched closely as China grapples with rising anxiety about AI-driven unemployment, and the court affirmed that existing labour protections cover workers displaced by automation.",
            "url": "https://www.scmp.com/tech/tech-trends/article/3352327/ai-cost-cutting-not-legal-excuse-fire-workers-chinese-court-says",
            "publisher": {
